<body lang="md">
# Hello, Dreego

Welcome to the {{ siteName }} blog. This post is written as real Markdown inside a Markdown body section, and the v0.3 md processor turns it into HTML at generation time.

## What shipped

The v0.2 release delivered the render foundation, and v0.3 wired up Markdown bodies. Together they make writing content pages feel like writing a document, not a template.

- Typed server sections stay the single source of truth
- Markdown bodies keep Dreego constructs intact
- Generated output stays close to ordinary Go and net/http

{#if showNote}
This sentence only renders when `showNote` is true — a Dreego condition living inside Markdown.
{/if}

> A note: Markdown can contain Dreego conditions. This blockquote is plain Markdown, converted to a blockquote element by the md processor.

## A small example

Inline code like `dreego generate` and a fenced block:

```go
func main() {
    println("hello, dreego")
}
```

## Next steps

Read about the [render foundation](/posts/rendering-foundation) or the [Markdown body feature](/posts/markdown-in-the-body).
</body>
